<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wadai War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1909–1911</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai</a> War was the French conquest of the Sultanate of Wadai in present-day eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a>. French troops took the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abeche">Abéché</a> in 1909 and drove out <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Dud Murra, who fought on with support from the neighbouring Masalit sultanate. Despite French defeats at the hands of the Masalit in 1910, Dud Murra surrendered in 1911, and Wadai was absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-equatorial-africa">French Equatorial Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wadai-war.jpg" alt="Wadai War" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Submission_of_Sultan_Dudmurrah_of_Wadai_(1911).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
